age 12 x 9 1/4 inches ^Sheet 14 7/8 x 11 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"cr_remarks_1999","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/cr_remarks_1999"}],"content":["Not recorded Whitney Archive, Downtown Gallery Archive, Abiquiú Notebooks. See cat. no. 241. (Source: Lynes, 1999)"],"type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"provenance_narrative","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/provenance_narrative"}],"content":"1918, Artist; 1991, Juan Hamilton; 1991 Acquired by gift from Juan Hamilton \n(Source: Sheldon Museum of Art, University of Nebraska–Lincoln, 2025)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Artist(s)","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_artist"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Complete","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_complete"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe. Untitled (Leah), 1918. Watercolor on paper, Image 12 x 9 1/4 inches ^Sheet 14 7/8 x 11 inches. Sheldon Museum of Art, University of Nebraska–Lincoln. Sheldon Museum of Art, University of Nebraska–Lincoln, Gift of anonymous donor, U-4423.1991. © Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"credit line","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026687"}],"content":"Sheldon Museum of Art, University of Nebraska–Lincoln, Gift of anonymous donor, U-4423.1991","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Measurement Description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/measurement_description"}],"content":"Image 12 x 9 1/4  inches \nSheet 14 7/8 x 11 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Copyright","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_copyright"}],"content":"© Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Holding Institution","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_instituion"}],"content":"Sheldon Museum of Art, University of Nebraska–Lincoln","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"extended_medium_description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/extended_medium_description"}],"content":"Watercolor on medium thick, cream, moderately textured paper; Watermark: Blind stamp at corner, STRATHMORE with thistle\n(Source: Paper Survey researched by Judith C. Walsh and published in Lynes, 1999.)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"Depicts Leah Harris, a food demonstrator in southwestern Texas, with whom O'Keeffe became friends in 1917. Minimalist forms come together to portray a woman with dark hair bending over. She stands on a surface denoted by a single curved line. The image contrasts with the plain white paper surrounding it.","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[{"digitally_shown_by":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/858958/full/full/0/default.jpg","type":"DigitalObject"}],"classified_as":[{"_label":"Digital Image","id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300215302","type":"Type"}],"digitally_available_via":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/858958"}],"conforms_to":[{"id":"http://iiif.io/api/image","type":"InformationObject"}],"format":"application/ld+json;profile='http://iiif.io/api/image/2/context.json'","type":"DigitalService"}],"type":"DigitalObject"}],"type":"VisualItem"}],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}